WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:14.973
Unit thirteen: Emphatic Structures. Today you will intensify meaning with so...that and such...that.

4
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:18.088
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.138
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:23.903
So...that.

7
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:28.321
So...that means a pattern for a result after an adjective.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.835
It was so cold that we stayed in.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.882
Your turn. Say: So...that.

10
00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:37.653
So...that.

11
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:39.534
Such...that.

12
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.687
Such...that means a pattern for a result after a noun.

13
00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:46.434
It was such a cold day that we stayed in.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.609
Your turn. Say: Such...that.

15
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.619
Such...that.

16
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:55.268
What a.

17
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:58.492
What a means an exclamation about a noun.

18
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:00.038
What a view!

19
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.314
Your turn. Say: What a.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:06.970
What a.

21
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:09.414
Emphatic exclamation.

22
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:13.902
Emphatic exclamation means a strong outcry.

23
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.354
An emphatic exclamation.

24
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.473
Your turn. Say: Emphatic exclamation.

25
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.136
Emphatic exclamation.

26
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:27.198
Intensifier.

27
00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:30.845
Intensifier means a word that adds strength.

28
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.624
Extremely is an intensifier.

29
00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:36.915
Your turn. Say: Intensifier.

30
00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.197
Intensifier.

31
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.276
Degree emphasis.

32
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:46.759
Degree emphasis means stressing how much.

33
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.630
Degree emphasis.

34
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:52.403
Your turn. Say: Degree emphasis.

35
00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.628
Degree emphasis.

36
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.744
Strong reaction.

37
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.400
Strong reaction means a powerful feeling.

38
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:04.426
A strong reaction.

39
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:08.563
Your turn. Say: Strong reaction.

40
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.819
Strong reaction.

41
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:14.747
Heightened effect.

42
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.411
Heightened effect means an effect made stronger.

43
00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:20.331
A heightened effect.

44
00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:23.824
Your turn. Say: Heightened effect.

45
00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.504
Heightened effect.

46
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.067
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:38.285
Visal, how can we show that something was extremely cold and made us stay in?

48
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:53.242
It was so cold that we stayed in. So + adjective + that expresses a degree that causes a result. With a noun phrase, use such: It was such a cold day that we stayed in.

49
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.024
What about exclamations?

50
00:02:57.117 --> 00:03:05.962
What a cold day! uses what with a noun, and How cold it was! uses how with an adjective. They show strong reactions.

51
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.376
Can we invert them?

52
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:22.378
Yes, for stronger emphasis in formal style: So cold was the night that we stayed in. Such was her talent that everyone listened. The inversion creates a heightened effect.

53
00:03:23.533 --> 00:03:25.080
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:33.268
Grammar focus: Emphatic result: so plus adjective plus that-clause; such plus a plus noun plus that-clause.

55
00:03:33.568 --> 00:03:34.755
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.461
It was so cold that we stayed in.

57
00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.744
It was such a cold day that we stayed in.

58
00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.009
Such was her talent that everyone listened.

59
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:52.623
So + adjective and such + a + noun both lead to a that-clause. Fronting so or such adds formal, dramatic emphasis.

60
00:03:53.383 --> 00:03:57.429
Be careful! Don't say: It was so a cold day that I slept.

61
00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:02.202
Say: It was such a cold day that I slept.

62
00:04:02.502 --> 00:04:04.107
Use such before a noun.

63
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.541
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:10.077
A Remarkable Performance.

65
00:04:10.377 --> 00:04:13.550
It was such a moving performance that nobody left early.

66
00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:17.973
The music was so beautiful that many people cried.

67
00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:20.955
What a talented young pianist she is!

68
00:04:21.967 --> 00:04:24.465
So great was her skill that the crowd stood up.

69
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.128
These structures show the strength of an impression.

70
00:04:29.233 --> 00:04:33.026
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:33.883 --> 00:04:36.080
It was blank cold that we stayed in.

72
00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.569
A, so. B, such. C, too.

73
00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.750
The answer is A: so.

74
00:04:45.883 --> 00:04:48.092
It was blank a long day that I slept.

75
00:04:48.392 --> 00:04:51.569
A, so. B, such. C, very.

76
00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.761
The answer is B: such.

77
00:04:57.917 --> 00:04:59.847
Which exclamation is correct?

78
00:05:00.147 --> 00:05:04.334
A, What a view!. B, How a view!. C, What view a!.

79
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.062
The answer is A: What a view!.

80
00:05:11.217 --> 00:05:14.006
So great was her skill is an blank structure.

81
00:05:14.306 --> 00:05:18.075
A, inverted. B, negative. C, passive.

82
00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:23.540
The answer is A: inverted.

83
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:27.774
According to the reading, what did the crowd do?

84
00:05:28.074 --> 00:05:31.275
A, stood up. B, left. C, slept.

85
00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:36.473
The answer is A: stood up.

86
00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:40.470
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:41.317 --> 00:05:44.930
Write a sentence using 'so...that' to show a strong effect.

88
00:05:53.717 --> 00:05:55.020
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:06.554
The film was so exciting that I forgot to eat my popcorn. It was such a moving story that many people cried. I use so and such to show how strong the effect was.

90
00:06:06.854 --> 00:06:08.494
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:09.383 --> 00:06:17.957
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and emphatic result: so plus adjective plus that-clause; such plus a plus noun plus that-clause.

92
00:06:18.257 --> 00:06:23.301
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:26.543
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:26.843 --> 00:06:29.832
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

